<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 26 April, from 1336 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petrarch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1336">1336 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">690 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Petrarch climbs Mont Ventoux for the view</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch">Petrarch</a> climbed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mont-ventoux">Mont Ventoux</a> in Provence, by his own account simply to see the view from the summit. His letter describing it is often cited as an early sign of a new attitude to nature.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Shakespeare is baptised in Stratford-upon-Avon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The parish register of Holy Trinity Church records the baptism of 'Gulielmus filius Johannes Shakspere'. It is the earliest documentary record of the playwright.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Wilkes Booth is cornered and killed in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Union troops trapped Lincoln's assassin in a tobacco barn and set it alight; Booth was shot by Sergeant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Corbett and died within hours. It ended a twelve-day manhunt.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1937">1937 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German and Italian aircraft bomb Guernica</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/condor-legion">Condor Legion</a>, with Italian support, bombed the Basque town on market day, killing hundreds of civilians. The attack inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-picasso">Picasso</a>'s painting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guernica">Guernica</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1986">1986 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Reactor explodes at the Chernobyl nuclear plant</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A safety test went wrong at reactor No. 4 in Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, causing an explosion and fire that spread radioactive fallout across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Over 100,000 people were evacuated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li></ol>
